backend/drm: show buffers in CPU memory by copying them

A software renderer draws into dumb buffers of the first GPU. Another GPU
can show them only by importing them over PRIME, as it can't copy them
without a renderer that imports DMA-BUFs, and a GPU that can't import them
shows nothing.

Accept buffers in CPU memory (WLR_BUFFER_CAP_DATA_PTR), and copy them into
buffers of each GPU's own with its multi-GPU renderer, which is created the
first time formats are asked for with DATA_PTR alone. A software renderer
then gets an shm allocator, and every GPU copies what changed. A compositor
that renders on the GPU never asks, and keeps its buffers.

